{"title": "Githyanki Barrier Disruptor", "pageid": 52710, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Githyanki_Barrier_Disruptor", "categories": ["Environmental objects"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Screen_Cr%C3%A8che_Y%27llek_Disruptor.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e7/Screen_Cr%C3%A8che_Y%27llek_Disruptor.jpg/300px-Screen_Cr%C3%A8che_Y%27llek_Disruptor.jpg.webp, /w/images/thumb/e/e7/Screen_Cr%C3%A8che_Y%27llek_Disruptor.jpg/450px-Screen_Cr%C3%A8che_Y%27llek_Disruptor.jpg.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/e/e7/Screen_Cr%C3%A8che_Y%27llek_Disruptor.jpg/600px-Screen_Cr%C3%A8che_Y%27llek_Disruptor.jpg.webp 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/e/e7/Screen_Cr%C3%A8che_Y%27llek_Disruptor.jpg/300px-Screen_Cr%C3%A8che_Y%27llek_Disruptor.jpg.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/e/e7/Screen_Cr%C3%A8che_Y%27llek_Disruptor.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption>The Githyanki Barrier Disruptor</figcaption></figure>\n<p>The <b>Githyanki Barrier Disruptor</b> is an interactable object located in the <a href=\"/wiki/Cr%C3%A8che_Y%27llek\" title=\"Crèche Y'llek\">Crèche Y'llek</a> found underneath <a href=\"/wiki/Rosymorn_Monastery\" title=\"Rosymorn Monastery\">Rosymorn Monastery</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Involvement\">Involvement</span></h2>\n<p>Upon entering the <a href=\"/wiki/Captain%27s_Quarters\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Captain's Quarters\">Captain's Quarters</a> in the <a href=\"/wiki/Cr%C3%A8che_Y%27llek\" title=\"Crèche Y'llek\">Crèche Y'llek</a> an argument will occur between a <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/W%27wargaz\" title=\"W'wargaz\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/c/c3/Portrait_W%27wargaz.png/25px-Portrait_W%27wargaz.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/c/c3/Portrait_W%27wargaz.png/38px-Portrait_W%27wargaz.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/c/c3/Portrait_W%27wargaz.png/50px-Portrait_W%27wargaz.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Ch'r'ai W'wargaz\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/c/c3/Portrait_W%27wargaz.png/25px-Portrait_W%27wargaz.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/c/c3/Portrait_W%27wargaz.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/W%27wargaz\" title=\"W'wargaz\">Ch'r'ai W'wargaz</a> and <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Therezzyn\" title=\"Therezzyn\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/3/3f/Portrait_Therezzyn.png/25px-Portrait_Therezzyn.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/3/3f/Portrait_Therezzyn.png/38px-Portrait_Therezzyn.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/3/3f/Portrait_Therezzyn.png/50px-Portrait_Therezzyn.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Kith'rak Therezzyn\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/3/3f/Portrait_Therezzyn.png/25px-Portrait_Therezzyn.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/3/3f/Portrait_Therezzyn.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Therezzyn\" title=\"Therezzyn\">Kith'rak Therezzyn</a>. After W'wargaz leaves for the <a href=\"/wiki/Inquisitor%27s_chamber\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Inquisitor's chamber\">Inquisitor's Chamber</a> via an archway to the north, Therezzyn activates a barrier using the Githyanki Barrier Disruptor next to the archway. \n</p><p>It is possible to deactive the barrier once again by interacting with the Githyanki Barrier Disruptor and using the <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Gith_Shard\" title=\"Gith Shard\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/a/a1/MISC_Gith_Shard_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-MISC_Gith_Shard_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/a/a1/MISC_Gith_Shard_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-MISC_Gith_Shard_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/a/a1/MISC_Gith_Shard_Unfaded_Icon.png/40px-MISC_Gith_Shard_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/a/a1/MISC_Gith_Shard_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-MISC_Gith_Shard_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/a/a1/MISC_Gith_Shard_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Gith_Shard\" title=\"Gith Shard\">Gith Shard</a>. It is the only way to explore past the northern exit of this location.\n</p><p>Therezzyn carries the Gith Shard, thus requiring the party to retrieve the shard from her in order to proceed. The party can offer to show the <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-story\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mysterious_Artefact\" title=\"Mysterious Artefact\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/1d/Mysterious_Artefact_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Mysterious_Artefact_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/1d/Mysterious_Artefact_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Mysterious_Artefact_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/1d/Mysterious_Artefact_Unfaded_Icon.png/40px-Mysterious_Artefact_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/1d/Mysterious_Artefact_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Mysterious_Artefact_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/1/1d/Mysterious_Artefact_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Mysterious_Artefact\" title=\"Mysterious Artefact\">Mysterious Artefact</a> to the Kith’rak or hide its presence through a <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/30px-D20.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/40px-D20.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Deception Check\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/13/D20.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Deception\" title=\"Deception\">Deception</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Ability_check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ability check\">Check</a>. If the party attempt to give her the artefact, Therezzyn opens the barrier to the Inquisitor's Chamber willingly. If the party withhold the information, the shard can either be acquired through pickpocketing or by killing the captain and looting it off her body.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714213915\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1394/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 10214/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 2109/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 19/200\nExpensive parser function count: 2/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/1000\nLua time usage: 0.015/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 914271/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   29.423      1 -total\n 46.64%   13.724      2 Template:SmRarityItem\n 4